From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The follower finishes its step when the game stops everyone
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A trainer who sees the player as they step into its sight starts its
script on that step, and the script's lock pauses every map object's
movement. The follower had set off on its own step after the player in
the same frame: its tile was the one beside the player, but paused, its
picture stayed on the tile it set off from, two tiles from the player,
while the trainer came over and through the battle's start. The step is
now finished first, as the game does for the partner who walks with the
player (ScrCmd_LockAll): unpaused till it stands, then paused as the rest
while the player is.

---
diff --git a/src/port_follower.c b/src/port_follower.c
index dba2a49b..6c2addae 100644
--- a/src/port_follower.c
+++ b/src/port_follower.c
@@ -1236,7 +1236,7 @@ static void PortFollower_TakeBallKind(FieldSystem *fieldSystem)
 void PortFollower_Update(FieldSystem *fieldSystem)
 {
     static int sWait, sPlayerX, sPlayerZ, sNoRoom, sOwnStep;
-    static BOOL sScriptStarted;
+    static BOOL sScriptStarted, sEndsStep;
     static MapObject *sLast;
     MapObject *mapObj, *player;
     int graphicsID = 0, x, z, dx, dz;
@@ -1322,6 +1322,27 @@ void PortFollower_Update(FieldSystem *fieldSystem)
         }
     }
 
+    // Stopped by the game (a script's lock: everyone's movement paused) as
+    // it set off on a step after the player, it stood where it set off
+    // from, a tile further back, two from the player, while the trainer who
+    // had seen them came over (Route 204, Aroma Lady Taylor, a photo of
+    // 2026-11-06: on the PC its tile was the one by the player, its picture
+    // a tile behind it). That step is finished first, as the game does for
+    // the partner who walks with the player (ScrCmd_LockAll): it goes on
+    // till it stands, then stops as the rest.
+    if (mapObj != NULL && sIn == 0 && sInWhy == NULL && sOut == POP_FRAMES && !sEndsStep
+        && MapObject_IsMoving(mapObj) && MapObject_IsMovementPaused(mapObj)) {
+        MapObject_SetPauseMovementOff(mapObj);
+        sEndsStep = TRUE;
+        NitroPort_Log("[follower] stopped by the game in a step: the step finished first");
+    } else if (sEndsStep && (mapObj == NULL || !MapObject_IsMoving(mapObj))) {
+        if (mapObj != NULL && MapObject_IsMovementPaused(player)) {
+            MapObject_SetPauseMovementOn(mapObj); // (as the rest, while they're stopped)
+        }
+
+        sEndsStep = FALSE;
+    }
+
     if (mapObj != NULL && sIn > 0) {
         // Going in: smaller each frame, then gone.
         sIn--;
